# 3-Layer Calculator App (Spring Boot + MongoDB) with CI/CD

This is a calculator web app made using Spring Boot, built with a proper 3-layer architecture. It does basic calculations (add, subtract, multiply, divide) and saves every calculation in MongoDB.

I also set up a full CI/CD pipeline for this project using Jenkins and Docker, so the whole thing builds and deploys automatically.

## 3-Layer Architecture

```
Presentation Layer  ->  Business Layer  ->  Database Layer
  (Thymeleaf UI)         (Service/Logic)      (MongoDB)
```

- **Presentation Layer** – HTML + Thymeleaf, takes input from the user
- **Business Layer** – Spring Boot controller + service, does the actual calculation
- **Database Layer** – MongoDB, stores the calculation history

## Tech Used

- Java 21
- Spring Boot
- Spring MVC
- Spring Data MongoDB
- Thymeleaf
- Maven
- MongoDB
- Docker
- Jenkins
- Git & GitHub
- Ubuntu Server

## CI/CD Pipeline

```
Push code to GitHub -> Jenkins builds project -> Maven creates jar ->
Docker image built -> Image pushed to Docker Hub -> Deployed on Ubuntu server ->
Spring Boot + MongoDB containers run
```

Jenkins does the whole thing automatically whenever I push new code — I don't have to build or deploy anything manually.

## Project Structure

```
src/main/java
